// empty-hull-child.csg — a `hull()` with one child that evaluates to NOTHING.
//
// The hull path tessellates each child to collect its vertices, and
// `tessellateShape` on an empty compound is the documented module-abort case
// (`BRepMesh_IncrementalMesh_2` on a shape with no sub-shapes →
// `wasmTable.get(...) is not a function`). A real design reaches this easily —
// any hull whose child is a `difference()` that cut itself away — so the empty
// child must be skipped and the hull built from what remains.
//
// Expected: loads successfully, 1 solid, volume 64 (the hull of the 4³ cube;
// the empty child contributes no points, silently — there is nothing to
// report about a child that legitimately evaluates to nothing).
group() {
  hull() {
    cube(size = [4, 4, 4], center = true);
    difference() {
      cube(size = [2, 2, 2], center = true);
      cube(size = [8, 8, 8], center = true);
    }
  }
}
